      "raw": "<p>They do if you use an attack+1 token to negate an attack-1 token. &nbsp;Attack -1 tokens just have to be used on your next attack. &nbsp;Attack +1 tokens are your choice to use on an stack against a specific target</p><p>edit: I&#39;ve looked at rulebook and see no mention of them automatically canceling each other out. &nbsp; While it is Luther listing that as a response, he is wrong that it is in the rulebook. &nbsp;</p>",
